From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:21:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: meson: vdec: HEVC and VP9 reference compressed pictures
 on G12A

At 3840x2160 the S905L3's VP9 decoder spends 19 ms on a picture, a
50 fps ceiling under its 4K60 rating: an 8-bit stream's references were
uncompressed, as only 10-bit, downscaled, compressed-CAPTURE and
non-64-aligned pictures referenced compressed ones. On G12A and later,
where the compressed references sit behind the decoder's MMU, they now
always do, and the double write gives CAPTURE its uncompressed picture,
the path those cases already take. fbc_reference=0 keeps the old rule.

On the S905L3 VP9 at 3840x2160 decodes at 67 fps in place of 46, HEVC
at 53 in place of 32, bit-identical to software.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/vdec/codec_hevc_common.h b/vdec/codec_hevc_common.h
index 04eef3d..a975528 100644
--- a/vdec/codec_hevc_common.h
+++ b/vdec/codec_hevc_common.h
@@ -37,13 +37,16 @@ struct codec_hevc_common {
 };
 
 /*
- * Returns 1 if references are compressed: 10-bit, a downscaled or a compressed CAPTURE, or a
- * width the uncompressed write's 32-byte pitch and the references' 64-byte one disagree on
+ * Returns 1 if references are compressed: 10-bit, a downscaled or a compressed CAPTURE, a width
+ * the uncompressed write's 32-byte pitch and the references' 64-byte one disagree on, or on
+ * G12A and later always, where they take a fraction of the uncompressed ones' memory traffic
  */
 static inline int codec_hevc_use_fbc(struct amvdec_session *sess, int is_10bit)
 {
 	return is_10bit || sess->dw_ratio > 1 || amvdec_fbc_capture(sess) ||
-	       !IS_ALIGNED(sess->width, 64);
+	       !IS_ALIGNED(sess->width, 64) ||
+	       (amvdec_fbc_reference &&
+		sess->core->platform->revision >= VDEC_REVISION_G12A);
 }
 
 /* Returns 1 if CAPTURE gets the decoder's second, uncompressed write */
diff --git a/vdec/vdec.c b/vdec/vdec.c
index 2bca56a..b06b814 100644
--- a/vdec/vdec.c
+++ b/vdec/vdec.c
@@ -37,6 +37,11 @@ struct dummy_buf {
 #define VDEC_FHD_PIXELS (1920 * 1088)
 #define VDEC_MAX_BUFFERS_UHD 16
 
+bool amvdec_fbc_reference = true;
+module_param_named(fbc_reference, amvdec_fbc_reference, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(fbc_reference,
+		 "HEVC, VP9 on G12A and later: compressed references behind an uncompressed CAPTURE");
+
 unsigned int amvdec_capture_max_width;
 module_param_named(capture_max_width, amvdec_capture_max_width, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(capture_max_width,
diff --git a/vdec/vdec.h b/vdec/vdec.h
index 776a628..ed7eb28 100644
--- a/vdec/vdec.h
+++ b/vdec/vdec.h
@@ -470,6 +470,7 @@ static inline u32 amvdec_ref_height(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 
 u32 amvdec_dw_ratio(struct amvdec_session *sess, u32 width, u32 height);
 
+extern bool amvdec_fbc_reference;
 extern unsigned int amvdec_capture_max_width;
 extern unsigned int amvdec_capture_max_height;
 
